# ai-defense-cli

Public Go CLI (`aid-cisco-cli`) for Cisco AI Defense: `model-scan`, `mcp-scan`, `ai-bom`.
No UI, database, or backend services in this repo.

## Stack

- **Go** — Cobra commands, HTTP SDK client, exit-code contract
- **Embedded Python** — relocatable CPython + packaged `cisco-aibom` for local AIBOM analysis (`internal/embedded/python/`)

## Commands

```bash
make build-go              # Go only (stub python)
make bundle build-embed    # Go + embedded CPython/aibom
make test vet
```

`BUILD_MODE=go|full` on `make build`. See `Makefile` and `scripts/README.md`.

## Agent workflow

- **Plan first** for migrations and contract changes (use Plan Mode or `spec-driven-dev` skill)
- **Rules** = always-on conventions (this file + go / python rules)
- **Skills** = on-demand workflows in `.cursor/skills/` (`spec-driven-dev`, `pr-review`, `debug-and-fix`)
- **Plans** — local only under `.cursor/plans/` (gitignored; do not commit)
- Read `CONTEXT.md` for migration status before large changes

## Conventions

- Feature branches off `main`; avoid direct commits to `main`
- Config resolution: flags > env > TOML
- Exit codes: see `internal/clierror` and `docs/architecture/ai-defense-cli.md`
- Never hardcode or log API keys
- Minimize diff scope; match existing patterns in `internal/cli/`, `internal/`, `api/`
